41 MX c=M | A Reserved reference graph plus its record.
  - XP m=RA rel=ARC-001,ARC-020,ARC-028 | A reference edge outside the accepted decisions is Reserved, even when architecturally legal.
    s: An allowed inward reference is added without approval: ARC-001 is satisfied; K1's check reports an error.
  - XW m=M rel=GOV-017 | The approval is recorded as an accepted decision edge.
    s: A reference approved in chat with no recorded edge: GOV-017 is satisfied; K1's check reports an error.
42 MX c=M | The same pair, at the guard.
  t: dependency and project-reference commands
  e: Recorded approval for every edge.
  r: PreToolUse deny semantics read statically (C10); the reported drift is the same reference-graph reading
  - XP m=RA rel=ARC-020,GOV-017 | Reference commands are blocked unless every discovered edge is an accepted decision.
    s: An allowed inward reference is added by command without approval: ARC-001 is satisfied; K1's guard blocks it.
  - XW m=MN rel=DEP-003 | Dependency guards block before execution.
    s: A dependency command that satisfies DEP-003 and DEP-004 in a form the classifier blocks: the policies are satisfied; K1's guard stops it first.
43 MX c=M | The same pair, at the guard.
  r: PreToolUse deny semantics read statically (C10)
  - XP m=RA rel=ARC-001,ARC-020,ARC-028 | Reference commands are blocked unless every named edge is approved.
    s: An allowed inward reference is added by command without approval: ARC-001 is satisfied; K1's guard blocks it.
  - XW m=M rel=GOV-017 | The edge is recorded as 'From -> To' in the decision register's Accepted decisions.
    s: A reference approved in chat with no recorded edge: GOV-017 is satisfied; K1's guard blocks it.
44 NN c=M rel=WF-007 | Reported uncertainty about which tools the post checks cover; a coverage fact.
45 XW m=M c=M rel=PST-008,PST-010,TST-009 | Same reading as M, M1, L1 and K0: a Stop block that requires a response.
